**Definition 30.2 (the specific restoration implication).** A
maximum-of-small-menu restoration claim with parameters $k_D$ and
$A_D\ge1$ asserts

$$
M_1(D)\le A_DH_D(k_D).
\tag{GDB.121}
$$

It includes any proposal that separately solves public menus of size
at most $k_D$ and then restores a full-menu code whose cardinality is
at most $A_D$ times the largest of those optima. Such a largest value
is at most $H_D(k_D)$, so that proposal implies (GDB.121).
This definition concerns a numerical implication, independent of the
method used to obtain the constituent controllers. It does not assert
that any credited supplier makes this claim.

